@startuml qwen3tts-speedup
title <b>qwen3tts: what buys 5x realtime</b>\nmeasured end to end on a 4763-word article: 201 segments, 28m 31s of audio, one M4 / 16 GB, f16

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 15
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #6B7A88
  BackgroundColor #EDF1F5
}
skinparam noteFontSize 12

rectangle "text -> segments" as SEG
rectangle "ICL prompt\nref codes + spk" as PROMPT
rectangle "**scheduler**\n48 lanes" as SCHED #DDF3E0
rectangle "**talker**\n0.128  (64%)" as TALKER #DDF3E0
rectangle "**codec**\n0.071  (36%)" as CODEC #DDF3E0
rectangle "24 kHz WAV\n**0.200 = 5.0x**" as WAV #D6E9F8

SEG --> PROMPT
PROMPT --> SCHED
SCHED --> TALKER : "48 lanes"
TALKER --> CODEC : "[T, 16] codes"
CODEC --> WAV

note right of SCHED #DDF3E0
  shape buckets
  length sort
  chunk to 48
end note

note right of TALKER #DDF3E0
  f16, not q8_0      <b>7.4x</b> vs 1.1x
  batched decode     48 lanes
  in-place KV        -112 MB/step
  folded tables      -126 MB/frame
  512-frame cap
end note

note right of CODEC #DDF3E0
  one call per utterance
  300 + 25 frame chunks
  fused NLC kernels
end note

note left of SCHED #FBDDDD
  <b>cliff at 56 lanes</b>
  RTF 0.701, 621 s sys
  swap, not compute
end note

note left of TALKER #FDEBD0
  <i>beyond 5x</i>
  lane refill
end note

note left of CODEC #FDEBD0
  <i>beyond 5x</i>
  torch-parity kernels
  (1.7-2.2x behind torch)
end note

note bottom of WAV #FFFDF0
  |= lanes |= talker |= codec |= RTF |= |
  | 24 | 0.162 | 0.071 | 0.235 | 4.3x |
  | <b>48</b> | <b>0.128</b> | 0.071 | <b>0.200-0.202</b> | <b>5.0x</b> |
  | 56 | 0.624 | 0.076 | 0.701 | cliff |
  | 64 | 0.574 | 0.072 | 0.647 | cliff |

  Per lane, in isolation, cost was still falling at 64 (~0.4 ms per added lane from 16 up).
  The wall is memory, not arithmetic: 48 lanes peak at 14.8 GB, 56 at 19.0 GB on a 16 GB machine.
  Canary 59.4 ms; the 24-lane baseline re-measured 0.235 -> 0.237 after 30 min of load, and 48
  re-measured 0.200 -> 0.202, so these are ratios within one thermal state.
  green measured, amber projected
end note

@enduml
